Z||000005||FieroKyle||11-10-2001||12:29 AM||||And the thing is, my Fiero is in really good shape, and my Buick has no rust, rally rims which came stock on it, a lot of pealing top coat of paint on the side, and not a whole bunch of miles.<P>I just figured out how to post pics, so heres a few of my Fiero.....<P> <IMG SRC="http://photos.onebigvillage.com/pubimage.asp?id_=63106"> <BR> <IMG SRC="http://photos.onebigvillage.com/pubimage.asp?id_=63110"> <BR> <IMG SRC="http://photos.onebigvillage.com/pubimage.asp?id_=63111"> <P>Notice the Goodyear Eagles rather then those crappy Kelly's that I bought the car with, LOL, a much better tire.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"><P> <IMG SRC="http://photos.onebigvillage.com/pubimage.asp?id_=63201"> <P> <IMG SRC="http://photos.onebigvillage.com/pubimage.asp?id_=63202"> <P>Sorry, got carried away with pics.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"> But I mean, like how can they make fun of it? Its in mint fricken condition. Interior is great too. You all may see the silver paint missing on the front bumper there. The whole front end has been painted this summer.||||reg||1
Z||000006||BC-GT||11-10-2001||12:36 AM||||Jealousy, insecurity. Seriously, it's different, it's cool.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif">:<P>------------------<BR>Darryl Martin<BR>1985 GT <BR>   <IMG SRC="http://www.imagestation.com/picture/pf251a969c96964ef15691e97e7ac4489/feb64e3a.jpg.orig.jpg"> ||||reg||1
Z||000007||Formula88||11-10-2001||02:02 AM||||Sweet ride, man.  No matter how cool you or your ride is, some people will be jerks just because they can. <P>Oh, the Grand National was never the fastest car in the "world."  In 1987, the Grand National was the fastest car sold in the U.S.  That exempts European only exotics that would blow it's doors off.  Faster than the 87 Vette.  While they were worrying about the Fiero, a Buick whooped their butt!  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif"> I was fortunate enough to buy an 87 GN brand new in the Fall of 87 (right after the stock market crash in October of 87).  That was one fast car!  But my Formula is more fun to drive.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif">  <P>The only car I've ever owned that came anywhere near as fun to drive as my Fiero was my 72 Trans Am.  But then, with a 455HO, it's hard for it NOT to be fun.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif">  Someone likened the MR2 vs. Fiero as the MR2 was a scalpel and the Fiero was an axe.  Along that analogy, the 72 Trans Am was a STEAMROLLER! ||||reg||14
Z||000008||BlackStang95||11-10-2001||02:35 AM||||Boomer that wasn't even remotely funny, but I'm glad you think I was cool in high school (I was).  I don't agree that the job anyone has indicates how good a person they are either.  I certainly don't think billy gates is cool.  Rich yes, smart probably, but that doesnt mean hes anyone to respect or admire.<P>I do remember the idiots in high school, most of all this guy who tried to tell me with a 100hp nos shot he hit 180 in his 78 (primered) camaro.  Good stuff.  <P>Kyle you look a little on the small side to do some serious ass kicking, but if you can go for it, if not bring an equalizer.  Don't take bs from people. ||||reg||1
Z||000009||Fierowrecker||11-10-2001||07:09 AM||||Hey Kyle!<BR>Don't worry about the clowns whos opinion don't matter...<BR>For you to own two vehicles, while in high school is an example of how mature YOU are...<BR>Not many people would put away their good car in the winter, and drive a beater (a good one at that!), just to prevent damage to the good car...<BR>As for the itiot that wanted to fight? It wasn't about the car... I am glad you didn't fight him, next time stear clear of the ropers (hemp smokers)...<BR>You will not get respect from a lot of people in school, but you will here!<BR>Which is more important to you?<BR>crash...||||reg||1
Z||000010||FieroKyle||11-10-2001||09:48 AM||||  <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by BlackStang95:<BR><B>Kyle you look a little on the small side to do some serious ass kicking, but if you can go for it, if not bring an equalizer.  Don't take bs from people. </B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>I am 6'0'', about 150 to 160. The kid that was causing trouble is about 5'10'', 140. skinnier than **** . That pic above is from last fall when I bought the car. I couldn't even drive yet. I have filled in a bit, and about 4to5'' taller. Plus the kid was drunk. I am pretty sure I could have taken him.<P>Yeah know it wouldn't have made a difference what I was driving. Probably better the Buick. He might have did something crazy to the Fiero and wrecked something on it.<p>[This message has been edited by FieroKyle (edited 11-10-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000011||WKDFIRO||11-10-2001||01:18 PM||||I think  that it is a good thing that you didn't have the Fiero at your confrontation. It doesn't sound like it would have mattered WHAT car you actually had, the guy was putting on a show for his underlings. I knew people like that in high school and believe me the best revenge on them is to simply go on and have a good life. This guy will eventually mess with someone badder than him that will stomp him in some way. <P>I specifically went to my Class reunions to see what these guys became and they became total losers almost without fail. Turns out they were completely unprepaired for life. <P>For me, whenever someone starts to talk trash about my Fiero I just start it up. With the modifications I had done to its 2.8 (years ago just before the first 3.4 conversions started coming out) it does the talking for me. It really seperates the little boy posers from the real racers who actually enjoy talking shop and not sh**. <P>Don't sink to this loser's level.<P>Formula88, I understand that the GN got the "World" title after it beat out the Ferrari at the time from 0-60. It was in one of the magazines, I want to say Car and Driver. It was a short lived title but one none the less. Years and years later the Syclone would be almost faster than a Ferrari and it was a truck!<P>||||reg||6
Z||000012||yo_sweet||12-17-2001||11:25 PM||||i get that from some people at school it's hard to ignore without getting mad then they say ya whatever when you explain why your paint is bad or soemthing like that, pure jelousy , then you see them on sundays driving there moms car lol eather way you'll be the better person in the end... it took me a bit to get over all the comment's but that's the way it is.<P>------------------<BR>1986 Fiero SE 2.8lv6<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/dance.gif">  <P><BR>www.geocities.com/acme_s2000/intro.html<BR>yo_sweet!||||reg||1
Z||000013||FieroRacer||12-17-2001||11:49 PM||||I once knew a guy who though a 1988 Hyundai Excel was a fast powerfull car!!!  He swore just because it had a manual and a 4 cylinder and light weight it could womp.  He also stated that no V8's could race in the illegal street drags because of weight, right before a Corvette laid a can of whoop ass down on a V6 Civic.  Look at me, I thought the excel was crap, the Daytona was fast for it's early design, the 4 cylinder fiero had torque, and the GT is nice!!!!||||reg||1
Z||000014||Fierokid87||12-18-2001||12:51 AM||||Yeah dont worry about these teens today.  If you know what you have in your car and they think its **** let them.  Cuzz latter on you can show them otherwise.  Weather it be racing, or just showing them that the Fiero is a great car for other reasons other then the fact they are pretty quick.<P>Scott<P>------------------<BR><FONT COLOR="red"> Fierokid's  Web site:</FONT><BR><FONT COLOR="white">http://www.angelfire.com/sports/sfiero</FONT><P><FONT COLOR="blue">AIM: Fierokid87<BR>ICQ: Fierokid</FONT><P>        <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/sfiero.JPG">   <BR>  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/fierokid-xmas-sig_1.gif"> ||||reg||1
Z||000015||watdge||12-18-2001||09:21 AM||||I'm still in school as well and see this sort of thing very often.  Folks at my school has this little organization called "Mixed up Kreations" where they slap a bunch of stickers on their cars, maybe some crome liner, shine --hubcaps--, and the new clear tail lights, calling them fast and basically laughin' at the other cars.  As far as I know none of them have fast cars.  2 neons, with the type R sticker mods, an explorer with straight pipes, and a chevy 1500 pickup with bullhorns on the hood.  Now, I have to admit, there are may folks in my school who actually appreciate true speed.  I knew a guy last year who owned an 87gt which I nearly bought.  But i'm finding more and more that "speed" is a trend that most all teens feel is in the imports.  Now don't get me wrong, I know that chrystler, Ford, and GM, are all domestic, but you wouldn't believe the number of honda's that are "fast" at my school.<P>*sigh* Anyway, I find that a lot of teens these days are set on the thought that "their car rules" and have very little appreciation for well engineered cars.  *laugh* I for one am humbled by owning an 88 ford taurus, with the 4 cylinder, that's right, 4.  *grin*  The only thing it's got going for it is a hole in the exaust pipe, making it sound more performance tunned.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"><P>Basically what I'm trying to say, is that, many teens are blinded by "new car" or "import" trends and won't be told other wise unless you show them.. and even then they are ignorant sometimes.  Don't worry about what they say, heck, if I had a fiero, I would just smile if I had a comment directed towards my car..(much like I do today) knowing it was the better of the two in most instances (well not from the taurus stand point).  Let that small stuff slide... and if it really nags you, get him out to a track or somethin'.  Over all they're either cocky, insecure, or jealous.  And that's all there is to it.    <P>Jeremy||||reg||4
Z||000016||kneebarx||12-18-2001||01:43 PM||||I'm surprised at the kind of negative responses that some of the people get on this forum regarding Fieros.  I live in New York, and I've had nothing but positive responses from people.  This was way before I knew anything about the Fiero.  Middle aged men would come up and ask me about it or compliment the car, and I had no idea why!  Well anyway, sorry to hear that you had to come across these type of people.  It's better to avoid and not fight those type of people b/c that exactly what they want.  They are bored and have nothing to do but to try to make their life more exciting by stirring up some trouble.  And of course they always seem to be with some other people.  Isn't that a weird coincidence?...Well, you did the right thing by not fighting with them.  Cuz thats exactly waht they want.||||reg||1
